 '<section class="panel" data-view="overview" role="tabpanel"><div class="stat-grid">'+box('Current running engine','None','Railway RHEN project has zero services')+box('Source candidate','V5 F1–F3f','Paper-only source, not merged or deployed')+box('Strategy status','Not validated','No production-quality alpha or promotion evidence')+'</div><div class="cols"><div class="card"><h2>Latest build</h2><p>The integrated successor source contains actual evidence journaling, scanner-origin verification, protected research input contracts, horizon outcomes and cost modeling. This Lab hosts a pinned <strong>source review</strong>, not a Python backend.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">PAPER ONLY</span><span class="tag">NO EXECUTION</span><span class="tag">NO BROKER CREDENTIALS</span><span class="tag">MANUAL PROMOTION</span></div><p class="fine" style="margin-top:16px">Reference: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="'+h(RHEN_REVIEW.source_pr)+'">Integrated RHEN PR #488 ↗</a></p></div><div class="card"><h2>Build status</h2>'+statuses+'</div></div><div class="card"><div class="subhead">NEXT RELEASE GATES</div><ul class="list"><li>Verified complete prospective market decision evidence</li><li>Independent archive restoration and source attestation</li><li>Real paper-session maturation and untouched holdout</li><li>Broker-specific authorization and separate safety review before any execution</li></ul></div></section>'+
 '<section class="panel" data-view="research" role="tabpanel" hidden><div class="card"><h2>Inside the integrated RHEN research build</h2><p>These are real source capabilities from the pinned V5 successor branch. They are development modules, not claims of a functioning hosted service.</p><div class="file-list">'+cards.map(([label,stage,desc])=>'<div class="source-file"><div><strong>'+h(label)+' · '+h(stage)+'</strong><small>'+h(desc)+'</small></div></div>').join('')+'</div><div class="note danger-note">Current evidence quality: <strong>AWAITING_INDEPENDENT_ATTESTATION.</strong> No executed fills, reliable equity curve, measured strategy alpha or autonomous promotion is available from this preview.</div></div></section>'+
 '<section class="panel" data-view="replay" role="tabpanel" hidden><div class="card"><h2>Paper Cost Lens</h2><p>A working browser-only cost-assumption calculator based on RHEN V5 <code>scorecard.py</code> logic: hypothetical net reference (bps) = hypothetical gross reference (bps) − spread − entry slippage − exit slippage − round-trip fees.</p><div class="note danger-note"><strong>Manual scenario, not real RHEN replay.</strong> Gross marks must be entered manually and are not sourced from market prices. Results are not trading profits, actual fills, historical validation or signals.</div><form id="costForm" autocomplete="off"><div class="subhead" style="margin-top:18px">ASSUMED ROUND-TRIP FRICTION · BASIS POINTS</div><div class="cost-form"><div class="field"><label for="spread">Spread (bps)</label><input data-label="Spread" id="spread" type="number" min="0" max="1000" step="any" value="5" required></div><div class="field"><label for="entry">Entry slippage (bps)</label><input data-label="Entry slippage" id="entry" type="number" min="0" max="1000" step="any" value="2" required></div><div class="field"><label for="exit">Exit slippage (bps)</label><input data-label="Exit slippage" id="exit" type="number" min="0" max="1000" step="any" value="2" required></div><div class="field"><label for="fees">Round-trip fees (bps)</label><input data-label="Round-trip fees" id="fees" type="number" min="0" max="1000" step="any" value="1" required></div></div><div class="cost-total"><span>Total assumed friction</span><strong id="roundtrip">—</strong></div><div class="horizon"><div class="subhead">OPTIONAL MANUAL HYPOTHETICAL GROSS MARKS</div><div class="cost-form"><div class="field"><label for="gross5">5-minute (bps)</label><input id="gross5" data-label="Five-minute gross" placeholder="No source mark" type="number" step="any"></div><div class="field"><label for="gross15">15-minute (bps)</label><input id="gross15" data-label="Fifteen-minute gross" placeholder="No source mark" type="number" step="any"></div><div class="field"><label for="gross60">60-minute (bps)</label><input id="gross60" data-label="Sixty-minute gross" placeholder="No source mark" type="number" step="any"></div></div></div><div class="results" aria-live="polite"><div class="result"><small>5m modeled net</small><strong id="net5">—</strong><em>PAPER SCENARIO</em></div><div class="result"><small>15m modeled net</small><strong id="net15">—</strong><em>PAPER SCENARIO</em></div><div class="result"><small>60m modeled net</small><strong id="net60">—</strong><em>PAPER SCENARIO</em></div></div><p id="costError" class="error" role="alert" aria-live="polite"></p><div class="buttons"><button type="submit">CALCULATE</button><button type="reset" class="secondary">RESET</button></div></form><p class="fine">Cost values are editable example assumptions only. All calculations are in this browser tab. Nothing is submitted, saved or connected to a broker.</p></div></section>'+
 '<section class="panel" data-view="source" role="tabpanel" hidden><div class="card"><h2>Source snapshot</h2><p>Browse the unchanged, exact-commit Python files underpinning the RHEN V5 research candidate. Files are text-only and protected by the Lab Access policy; opening them cannot run RHEN.</p><p class="caps">REPOSITORY</p><p><a href="https://github.com/anevum/rhen/tree/'+h(RHEN_REVIEW.source_commit)+'/next_rhen" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">anevum/rhen · successor source ↗</a></p><p class="caps">PINNED COMMIT</p><p class="digest">'+h(RHEN_REVIEW.source_commit)+'</p><div class="file-list">'+files+'</div><div class="note">The original RHEN source remains canonical. Future UI work can replace this read-only wrapper after a secure research runtime and per-member account boundary have been validated.</div></div></section>'+
 '</main><footer><span>ANEVUM LAB · PRIVATE SOURCE REVIEW · NOT DEPLOYED</span><span>RHEN '+h(RHEN_REVIEW.source_commit.slice(0,12))+'</span></footer></div></body></html>';
